 Judy makes in a week:\n   - She charges $15.00 per student.\n   - Total amount = 495 students * $15.00 per student = $7447.50.\n\n#### $7447.50","oracle":"Incorrect","verdicts":[{"key":"qwen3.5-122b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"phi4-14b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen3-14b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen2.5-72b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"llama3.3-70b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen3-8b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"gpt-oss-120b","budget":8192,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"phi4rp-14b","budget":8192,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"phi4r-14b","budget":8192,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"glm-4.5-air","budget":8192,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"phi4mi-3.8b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen3-4b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"llama3.1-8b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen2.5-7b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen3-1.7b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"phi4mr-3.8b","budget":8192,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"llama3.2-3b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"qwen2.5-1.5b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen2.5-3b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen3-0.6b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"deepseek-r1-distill-llama-70b","budget":8192,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"llama3.2-1b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"}]},{"dataset":"math","datasetName":"MATH","student":"qwen2.5-32b","studentName":"Qwen2.5-32B-Instruct-GPTQ-Int8","id":15,"question":"What is the smallest real number $x$ in the domain of the function $$g(x) = \\sqrt{(x-3)^2-(x-8)^2}~?$$","reference":"\\frac{11}{2}","answer":"5.5","reasoning":"To solve this problem, we first need to understand the domain of the function \\(g(x) = \\sqrt{(x-3)^2-(x-8)^2}\\). The expression under the square root, \\((x-3)^2-(x-8)^2\\), must be non-negative for \\(g(x)\\) to be a real number.\n\nLet's first simplify the expression under the square root:\n\n\\[\n(x-3)^2 - (x-8)^2\n\\]\n\nExpanding both squares, we get:\n\n\\[\n(x^2 - 6x + 9) - (x^2 - 16x + 64)\n\\]\n\nSimplifying further, we combine like terms:\n\n\\[\nx^2 - 6x + 9 - x^2 + 16x - 64 = 10x - 55\n\\]\n\nTherefore, the expression under the square root simplifies to:\n\n\\[\ng(x) = \\sqrt{10x - 55}\n\\]\n\nFor \\(g(x)\\) to be defined, the expression under the square root must be non-negative:\n\n\\[\n10x - 55 \\geq 0\n\\]\n\nSolving this inequality for \\(x\\):\n\n\\[\n10x \\geq 55\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx \\geq \\frac{55}{10}\n\\]\n\n\\[\nx \\geq 5.5\n\\]\n\nThus, the smallest real number \\(x\\) in the domain of \\(g(x)\\) is \\(5.5\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{5.5}\n\\]","oracle":"Correct","verdicts":[{"key":"qwen3.5-122b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"phi4-14b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"qwen3-14b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"qwen2.5-72b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"llama3.3-70b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen3-8b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"gpt-oss-120b","budget":8192,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"phi4rp-14b","budget":8192,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"phi4r-14b","budget":8192,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"glm-4.5-air","budget":8192,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"phi4mi-3.8b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen3-4b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"llama3.1-8b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen2.5-7b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"qwen3-1.7b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"phi4mr-3.8b","budget":8192,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"llama3.2-3b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"qwen2.5-1.5b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen2.5-3b","budget":10,"verdict":"Incorrect"},{"key":"qwen3-0.6b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"},{"key":"deepseek-r1-distill-llama-70b","budget":8192,"verdict":"Undefined"},{"key":"llama3.2-1b","budget":10,"verdict":"Correct"}]},{"dataset":"arc_challenge","datasetName":"ARC-Challenge","student"